From b97200d2bb4076ceed344050a030bcb66f8a3d90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gavin_darkglider <rbrown4014@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:14:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] core: modernize the build system and drop bundled
 libraries

Build against current autotools and toolchains.

- Replace the bundled zlib 1.2.3, libpng 1.2.18, libjpeg-6b and freetype
  2.3.5 copies (all with known CVEs; the kernel helper parses theme images
  as root at boot) and the klibc build with pkg-config detection of the
  system libraries.
- Link the kernel helper statically with 'pkg-config --static' by default
  (--disable-static-helper links it dynamically), and check at configure
  time that the static link actually works so a missing .a is reported
  with a hint instead of failing mid-build.  Same for fbsplashctl.
- AS_HELP_STRING, LT_INIT, AM_CPPFLAGS, subdir-objects, silent rules.
- Fix the default essential prefix ("//bin" paths).
- Fix the unit test and misc programs' include paths so 'make check'
  works.
- Build with -Werror for implicit declarations and pointer/int
  conversions, which GCC 14+ makes errors anyway.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
